---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/base-layout.astro"
import LegalArticle from "@/components/legal-article.astro"
import ExternalLinkIcon from "@/components/external-link-icon.astro"
import { routeUrl } from "@/i18n/url"
import { siteConfig } from "@/data/site"
import { getTranslations } from "@/i18n/translations"
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${siteConfig.name.brand} - Privacy Policy`}
  description={getTranslations("en").privacy.metaDescription}
  noindex
>
  <LegalArticle>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted">
      Last updated: <time datetime="2026-10-08">8 October 2026</time>
    </p>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>
      The controller under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) is {siteConfig.name.full}.
      You can find the full contact details, postal address and ways to contact me by email and
      phone in the{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href={routeUrl("en", "legal")}
      >
        Legal Notice
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>Website access and hosting</h2>
    <p>
      This website is hosted by Netlify, Inc. When you open a page, technically necessary data is
      processed. This includes your IP address, the time and destination of the request, and browser
      information. Netlify processes technical access data to deliver the website, investigate
      errors and prevent attacks. I do not export access logs or create my own visitor statistics.
    </p>
    <p>
      This processing makes the website available and secure. Its legal basis is Article 6(1)(f) of
      the GDPR. My legitimate interest is to operate a functional and secure website. For the
      central logging and monitoring of its service components, Netlify states in the data
      processing agreement linked below that logs are retained online for 90 days and offline for
      one year.
    </p>
    <p>
      Netlify may process data in the United States and other countries outside the European
      Economic Area. For transfers to the United States, Netlify's data processing agreement
      provides for the{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href="https://www.dataprivacyframework.gov/participant/6208"
      >
        EU-US Data Privacy Framework
        <ExternalLinkIcon />
      </a>
      , under which Netlify states it is certified. Where this mechanism does not apply, the
      agreement provides for EU Standard Contractual Clauses. For more information, see{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
      >
        Netlify's privacy notice
        <ExternalLinkIcon />
      </a>{" "}
      and the{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href="https://www.netlify.com/pdf/netlify-dpa.pdf"
      >
        data processing agreement
        <ExternalLinkIcon />
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>Contact by email</h2>
    <p>
      If you send us an email, we process your sender address, the message, any attachments, and the
      technical details to handle your inquiry. I use a mailbox provided by STRATO GmbH to receive,
      store and send email. There is no automatic forwarding to another mailbox and no contact form.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your inquiry relates to a contract or pre-contractual measures, the legal basis is Article
      6(1)(b) of the GDPR. For other inquiries, processing is based on Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR.
      My legitimate interest is to handle your inquiry and respond to you.
    </p>
    <p>
      Once an inquiry has been fully resolved, I delete the correspondence, including my replies,
      from the mailbox and trash. Records still needed for an ongoing matter or to meet statutory
      retention obligations are kept for as long as necessary. For more information about processing
      by STRATO, see{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href="https://www.strato.de/datenschutz/"
      >
        STRATO's privacy notice
        <ExternalLinkIcon />
      </a>{" "}
      and the{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href="https://www.strato.de/agb/avv/"
      >
        data processing agreement
        <ExternalLinkIcon />
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      The provider's recovery process is separate from this. According to STRATO, messages deleted
      from the mailbox, including the trash, can still be recovered for up to 30 days. For details,
      see the{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href="https://www.strato.de/faq/mail/wie-kann-ich-meine-geloeschten-e-mails-wiederherstellen/"
      >
        explanation of email recovery
        <ExternalLinkIcon />
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>Contact by phone</h2>
    <p>
      If you call me, I process your phone number, the time of the call and the information you
      provide to handle your inquiry. I use satellite Free, provided by sipgate GmbH, for telephone
      communication. I do not use voicemail, call recordings, transcriptions or AI summaries.
    </p>
    <p>
      If your inquiry relates to a contract or pre-contractual measures, the legal basis is Article
      6(1)(b) of the GDPR. For other inquiries, processing is based on my legitimate interest in
      handling your inquiry and responding to you under Article 6(1)(f) of the GDPR. If I store data
      to handle your inquiry, I delete it once your inquiry has been fully resolved, provided it is
      no longer needed and no statutory retention obligations apply.
    </p>
    <p>
      sipgate processes the connection data necessary for telephony, particularly the phone numbers
      involved and the start and end of a call. The call history used across devices is stored by
      sipgate. According to the provider, these entries are deleted when I delete them in the app or
      the contract ends. This is separate from data sipgate processes for billing or statutory
      retention obligations. For more information, see{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href="https://www.satellite.me/datenschutz/"
      >
        satellite's privacy notice
        <ExternalLinkIcon />
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2>Fonts, cookies, and analytics</h2>
    <p>
      The fonts, images and gallery are served with the website. Loading them does not connect to
      external font or image providers. This website does not set its own cookies or use analytics
      tools, embedded third-party content, comments or newsletters. The gallery uses neither local
      storage nor session storage. It uses the local browser history for image navigation.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You may request access to, rectification or erasure of, and restriction of processing of your
      personal data. Where the legal requirements are met, you also have a right to data
      portability. Where processing is based on legitimate interests, you may object on grounds
      relating to your particular situation. To exercise your rights, contact me using the details
      in the{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href={routeUrl("en", "legal")}
      >
        Legal Notice
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      You may lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory authority, particularly the{" "}
      <a
        class="site-link text-muted [font-family:inherit] hover:text-ink"
        href="https://www.lda.bayern.de/de/beschwerde.html"
      >
        Bavarian State Office for Data Protection Supervision (BayLDA)
        <ExternalLinkIcon />
      </a>
      . You retain the right to contact another supervisory authority competent under the GDPR.
    </p>
  </LegalArticle>
</BaseLayout>
